Republic of the Philippines DEPARTMENT OF THE INTERIOR AND LOCAL GOVERNMENT DILG-NAPOLCOM Building, EDSA corner Quezon Avenue, Quezon City W.v.v.dilg.gov.ph BIYAHENC PINO? -a.*kl NA PNAAD. MS. VICTORIA M. ZAMBRANO Department Manager Land Bank of the Philippines La Union Lending Center City of San Fernando, La Union Dear Ms. Zambrano: DILG Legal Opinion No. 30, S. 2014 01 Z014 This refers to your 13 May 2014 letter to DILG Region I Assistant Director Julie J. Daquioag, which was referred to the Central Office, requesting clarification on whether DILG MC No. 2013-47 shall be applicable in the event that the LGU's infrastructure project for bank financing includes the acquisition of motor vehicles as a component of the project. The following are the salient features of the LGU's infrastructure project as indicated in your letter : a) The contract amount of the infrastructure project includes the acquisition of vehicle to be acquired by the winning bidder-contractor. The said vehicle shall be solely used by the Municipal Engineer in supervising the construction. b) The acquisition of vehicle is not explicitly included in the LGU's Annual Investment Plan (AIP), Annual Procurement Plan (APP) and Project Procurement Management Plan (PPMP). Nevertheless, the infrastructure project wherein acquisition of vehicle is incorporated, is included in the LGU's AIP, APP, and PPMP. The following are the discussions relative to your query: DILG MC No. 2013-47 was issued by this Department pursuant to Administrative Order (AO) No. 233, s. 2008, as amended by AO No. 15, s. 2011 (hereinafter, AO 233, as amended), which aims to prohibit the acquisition and use of luxury vehicles by the government, as well as to provide a uniform and streamlined guidelines on government motor vehicles acquisition. Notably, motor vehicle acquisitions of all government agencies are governed by said issuance, except the following based on Section 3.0 thereof, to wit: Order: 3.1 "3.0 The following motor vehicles are not covered by this Those used for security reasons and purposes for President, Vice- President, Senate President, Speaker of the House Of Representatives and Chief Justice of the Supreme Court;

3.2 3.3 3.4 nicle donated by Foreign Governnlents ..nd Bilateral and Multilateral Institutions, of compliance with this Order is violative of the terms and conditions of such donation; Vehicles used for visiting dignitaries maintained by the Office of the President (OP)-Proper and the Department of Foreign Affairs; and Vehicles acquired for on-going projects funded from existing official development assistance programs;" As to the acquisition of motor vehicles by local government units (LGUs), the same is governed by Section 8.0 of AO 233, as amended, viz.: "8.0 Local Chief Executives, including Punong Barangays, are hereby authorized to approve the acquisition of the types of motor vehicles enumerated under Section 7.0 hereof to be sourced from their unencumbered local funds. However, for acquisition of said vehicles to be sourced from the national government funds under the General Appropriations Act, the LGII shall seek the approval of the Secretary of Budget and Management for motor vehicles under Section 7.0 or the Secretary of the Interior and Local Government for Other motor vehicles as provided under Section 9.0 hereof. " It should be emphasized that the acquisition of motor vefiicles of LGUs are not only governed by AO 233, as amended, but also the provisions of Republic Act No. 9184 (RA 9184) and its Implementing Rules and Regulations (IRR), and as other pertinent policy issuances, particularly on the source of fund to be utilized for the acquisition of the motor vehicle, keeping in mind the limitations on the use thereof. Anent the inclusion of the acquisition of motor vehicle in the contract amount of the infrastructure project, the same appears to circumvent RA 9184 and its IRR as it includes the undertaking to acquire the Municipal Engineer's service vehicle as part of the contractor's Scope of Work. While it may be true that the acquisition of motor vehicle was included as a component of the project, it is imperative to note that that procurement of goods and infrastructure projects are governed by different sets of guidelines and standards. Note the definition of "goods" and "infrastructure projects" under Section 5 (h) and (k) of RA 9184, to wit: "Section 5. Definition of Terms. — For purposes of this Act, the following terms or words and phrases shall mean or be understood as follows: xxx (h) Goods — refer to all items, supplies„ materials and general support services, except consulting services and infrastructure projects, which rnay be

needed in the ,nsaction of public businesses or in pursui, of any government undertaking, project or activity, whether in the nature of equipment, furniture, stationery, materials for construction, or personal property of any kind, including non-personal or contractual services such as the repair and maintenance ofequipment and furniture, as zpell as trucking, hauling, janitorial security, and related or analogous services, as well as procurement of materials and supplies provided by the procuring entity for such services. xxx (k) Infrastructure Projects - include the construction, improvement, rehabilitation, demolition, repair, restoration or maintenance of roads, bridges, railways, airports, seaports, comnlunication facilities, civil works components of infornmtion technology projects, irrigation, flood control and drainage, water supply, sanitation, sewerage and solid waste management systems, shore protection, energy/power and electrification facilities, national buildings, school buildings, hospital buildings and other related construction projects of the government. " In view thereof, it is clear that LGU acquisition of motor vehicles is subject to compliance with DILG MC No. 2013-47 and other issuances of this Department on the subject pursuant to the provisions of AO 233, as amended and other pertinent laws, rules and regulations thereto. It should be emphasized however that the discussions pertaining to RA 9184 and its IRR are not controlling and are not intended to supplant the GPPB's interpretation/opinion on the matter as the body mandated to ensure proper implementation of the government procurement law and it IRR and other rules and regulations pertaining to public procurement. Thank you. Very truly yours, AUSTERE A. PANADERO Undersecretary DILG.Ot,S1.G
